@node Commands
@section Commands

@table @code
@item M-x tandem
@findex tandem
Chat with Claude about the current project. Show this project's chat; else reattach to one still open in the daemon, as after Emacs restarted; else start one.  With prefix argument NEW, always start a new session.  To reopen an older chat, use @code{tandem-resume}.

@item M-x tandem-answer-permission
@findex tandem-answer-permission
Answer Claude's waiting permission question from any buffer.

@item M-x tandem-ask
@findex tandem-ask
Ask Claude QUESTION about the region, or the function or line at point. The question goes to the project's chat with the file, the lines and the code; the answer shows in the chat and in a note above the code.

@item M-x tandem-blame
@findex tandem-blame
Say who wrote the line at point. With prefix argument ALL, list every run of lines Claude wrote in this buffer, each a link to its lines.

@item M-x tandem-chat-allow
@findex tandem-chat-allow
Allow the permission request at point, once. For Claude's plan, open it instead: you approve it there.

@item M-x tandem-chat-allow-always
@findex tandem-chat-allow-always
Allow the permission request at point, and keep allowing it in this project. Claude Code saves the rule in the project's .claude/settings.local.json.

@item M-x tandem-chat-answer-permission
@findex tandem-chat-answer-permission
Answer the permission request at point, or the oldest one, from a menu.

@item M-x tandem-chat-apply-edit
@findex tandem-chat-apply-edit
Apply the proposed edit at point.

@item M-x tandem-chat-cancel
@findex tandem-chat-cancel
Stop Claude's current answer.

@item M-x tandem-chat-deny
@findex tandem-chat-deny
Deny the permission request at point.

@item M-x tandem-chat-deny-with-reason
@findex tandem-chat-deny-with-reason
Deny the permission request at point and tell Claude why.

@item M-x tandem-chat-next-input
@findex tandem-chat-next-input
Put the Nth next sent message in the composer, or empty it.

@item M-x tandem-chat-previous-input
@findex tandem-chat-previous-input
Put the Nth previous sent message in the composer.

@item M-x tandem-chat-reject-edit
@findex tandem-chat-reject-edit
Reject the proposed edit at point.

@item M-x tandem-chat-reject-edit-with-reason
@findex tandem-chat-reject-edit-with-reason
Reject the proposed edit at point and tell Claude why.

@item M-x tandem-chat-send
@findex tandem-chat-send
Send the composer's text to Claude.

@item M-x tandem-chat-send-reviews
@findex tandem-chat-send-reviews
Send your review of deferred edits to Claude, with whatever you typed.

@item M-x tandem-chat-show-edit
@findex tandem-chat-show-edit
Show the proposed edit at point in its file's buffer.

@item M-x tandem-chats
@findex tandem-chats
List every chat with Claude: project, branch, state, what waits, cost.

@item M-x tandem-chats-close
@findex tandem-chats-close
Close the chat on this line: its session ends; it stays in @code{tandem-resume}.

@item M-x tandem-chats-open
@findex tandem-chats-open
Show the chat on this line; one open only in the daemon is reattached.

@item M-x tandem-connect
@findex tandem-connect
Connect to the tandem daemon, starting it if it is not running.

@item M-x tandem-daemon-status
@findex tandem-daemon-status
Show the daemon's version, process id, uptime and connected clients.

@item M-x tandem-dashboard-apply
@findex tandem-dashboard-apply
Apply the hunk on this line.

@item M-x tandem-dashboard-apply-edit
@findex tandem-dashboard-apply-edit
Apply every waiting hunk of the edit the hunk on this line is part of.

@item M-x tandem-dashboard-ask
@findex tandem-dashboard-ask
Ask Claude about the hunk on this line.

@item M-x tandem-dashboard-reject
@findex tandem-dashboard-reject
Reject the hunk on this line, asking why.

@item M-x tandem-dashboard-reject-edit
@findex tandem-dashboard-reject-edit
Reject every waiting hunk of the edit the hunk on this line is part of.

@item M-x tandem-dashboard-show
@findex tandem-dashboard-show
Show the hunk on this line in its file.

@item M-x tandem-disconnect
@findex tandem-disconnect
Close the connection to the daemon and leave the daemon running.

@item M-x tandem-do
@findex tandem-do
Tell Claude to do CHOICE with the region, or the function or line at point. CHOICE is a name from @code{tandem-do-actions} or an instruction of your own. Claude's change comes as hunks in this buffer for you to review.  With PLAN (\[universal-argument]), Claude plans first, in an Org buffer you can edit.

@item M-x tandem-events-buffer
@findex tandem-events-buffer
Show the log of messages exchanged with the daemon.

@item M-x tandem-locations
@findex tandem-locations
Show the places of Claude's last xref lookup.

@item M-x tandem-magit-draft-message
@findex tandem-magit-draft-message
Have Claude write the commit message for what is staged. Claude reads the staged diff and, if the project has a chat, what was said there.  The answer replaces the message in this buffer.

@item M-x tandem-magit-stage-claude
@findex tandem-magit-stage-claude
Stage the hunks you accepted from Claude, and only those. A hunk is Claude's when every line it adds is one of Claude's coloured lines; a new file, when all of it is.  Lines Claude removed without adding any cannot be told from yours, and stay unstaged.  Files with unsaved changes are left alone.

@item M-x tandem-mention-insert
@findex tandem-mention-insert
Insert a mention of NAME, chosen from a menu.

@item M-x tandem-notes-restore
@findex tandem-notes-restore
Colour Claude's lines in this file from the nearest git note on it. Return how many lines were marked.

@item M-x tandem-notes-share
@findex tandem-notes-share
Share Claude's notes with REMOTE: fetch them from now on, and push yours. Fetched notes are kept apart from yours, so a fetch never overwrites notes you have not pushed; before pushing, the two are merged.

@item M-x tandem-notes-write
@findex tandem-notes-write
Write the note on COMMIT (HEAD by default) saying which lines are Claude's. Return the number of files in it; a commit with none of Claude's lines gets no note.

@item M-x tandem-org-send-subtree
@findex tandem-org-send-subtree
Send the Org subtree at point to Claude as a task. Claude's answer goes under the heading when it is done.  With PLAN (a prefix argument), Claude plans first, in an Org buffer you can edit.

@item M-x tandem-plan
@findex tandem-plan
Give Claude TASK in plan mode, to plan it without changing anything. The plan opens in an Org buffer for you to edit before Claude goes ahead.

@item M-x tandem-plan-approve
@findex tandem-plan-approve
Let Claude go ahead with the plan as it is in this buffer.

@item M-x tandem-plan-reject
@findex tandem-plan-reject
Tell Claude no to this plan, with REASON.

@item M-x tandem-popup-hide
@findex tandem-popup-hide
Close the popup.

@item M-x tandem-popup-show
@findex tandem-popup-show
Open the popup for the hunk at point now.

@item M-x tandem-resume
@findex tandem-resume
Reopen one of the current project's earlier chats with Claude.

@item M-x tandem-review
@findex tandem-review
List every hunk Claude proposed that waits for your decision.

@item M-x tandem-review-apply
@findex tandem-review-apply
Apply every waiting hunk of Claude's edit ID, or of the edit at point. Each hunk is one undo step.  The buffer is saved once, when it had no unsaved changes of yours and @code{tandem-review-autosave} is non-nil.

@item M-x tandem-review-apply-hunk
@findex tandem-review-apply-hunk
Apply the hunk at point, as one undo step. With prefix argument ALL, apply every waiting hunk of its edit.

@item M-x tandem-review-ask-hunk
@findex tandem-review-ask-hunk
Ask Claude QUESTION about the hunk at point before deciding on it. The edit goes back to Claude with your question: hunks you decided keep their decisions, the others are not applied, and Claude answers and may propose them again.  Its answer shows as a note where the hunk was.

@item M-x tandem-review-dismiss-note
@findex tandem-review-dismiss-note
Remove the note for edit ID, or every note in this buffer.

@item M-x tandem-review-next-hunk
@findex tandem-review-next-hunk
Move to the next hunk Claude proposed in this buffer.

@item M-x tandem-review-previous-hunk
@findex tandem-review-previous-hunk
Move to the previous hunk Claude proposed in this buffer.

@item M-x tandem-review-reject
@findex tandem-review-reject
Reject every waiting hunk of Claude's edit ID, or of the edit at point. Interactively, ask for REASON, an optional note Claude reads.

@item M-x tandem-review-reject-hunk
@findex tandem-review-reject-hunk
Reject the hunk at point, asking for REASON, an optional note for Claude. With prefix argument ALL, reject every waiting hunk of its edit.

@item M-x tandem-review-show
@findex tandem-review-show
Show the first waiting hunk of Claude's edit ID, or of the newest edit.

@item M-x tandem-review-toggle-note
@findex tandem-review-toggle-note
Fold or unfold the note for edit ID, or the nearest note above point.

@item M-x tandem-rewind
@findex tandem-rewind
Go back to before one of your messages: files and conversation. The files Claude changed in Emacs from then on return to how they were, Claude forgets that message and what came after, and the message is back in the composer.

@item M-x tandem-set-review-style
@findex tandem-set-review-style
Set how Claude's edits wait for you, to STYLE; see @code{tandem-review-style}.

@item M-x tandem-slash-refresh
@findex tandem-slash-refresh
Read again the slash commands Claude Code has for the chat BUFFER. BUFFER is the current one by default.  The answer comes later; you can keep typing.  Nothing happens without a connection to the daemon.

@item M-x tandem-stop-daemon
@findex tandem-stop-daemon
Stop the tandem daemon if it is running.

@item M-x tandem-suggest-accept
@findex tandem-suggest-accept
Insert the suggestion shown at point.

@item M-x tandem-suggest-now
@findex tandem-suggest-now
Ask Claude for a suggestion at point now, without waiting for a pause.

@item M-x tandem-worktree
@findex tandem-worktree
Make a git worktree NAME on a new branch NAME, and open its chat. The worktree goes next to the repository (see @code{tandem-worktree-directory}), from the commit you have checked out; a branch NAME that exists already is checked out there instead.

@item M-x tandem-worktree-remove
@findex tandem-worktree-remove
Remove the git worktree at PATH and close its chat. Refuse when it has changes not committed, unless FORCE (a prefix argument).  The branch stays.

@end table

@node Options
@section Options

@kbd{M-x customize-group RET tandem RET} lists them too.

@table @code
@item tandem-attribution-directory
@vindex tandem-attribution-directory
Default: @code{"/home/victory/.cache/tandem/attribut...}.  Directory holding, for each file, which of its lines Claude wrote. It is made private to you (mode 700).

@item tandem-attribution-ignore-whitespace
@vindex tandem-attribution-ignore-whitespace
Default: @code{t}.  Non-nil means a Claude line keeps its colour when only whitespace changes. Formatters and reindenting change whitespace on many lines at once.

@item tandem-attribution-persist
@vindex tandem-attribution-persist
Default: @code{t}.  Non-nil means remember Claude's lines after a file is closed.

@item tandem-author-color
@vindex tandem-author-color
Default: @code{"#d97757"}.  Colour blended into the background of Claude's lines, or nil. With nil, the face @code{tandem-author} is left as your theme sets it.

@item tandem-author-tint
@vindex tandem-author-tint
Default: @code{0.1}.  How much of @code{tandem-author-color} to blend in: 0 none, 1 all.

@item tandem-chat-flush-interval
@vindex tandem-chat-flush-interval
Default: @code{0.04}.  Seconds between screen updates while Claude writes.

@item tandem-chat-history-size
@vindex tandem-chat-history-size
Default: @code{100}.  Number of sent messages that \[tandem-chat-previous-input] can recall.

@item tandem-chat-window-width
@vindex tandem-chat-window-width
Default: @code{0.38}.  Width of the chat window: a fraction of the frame, or a number of columns.

@item tandem-chats-refresh
@vindex tandem-chats-refresh
Default: @code{1}.  Seconds between refreshes of the chats dashboard while it is shown.

@item tandem-claude-command
@vindex tandem-claude-command
Default: @code{nil}.  Path of the claude command, or nil to look for "claude" on variable @code{exec-path}.

@item tandem-daemon-command
@vindex tandem-daemon-command
Default: @code{nil}.  Command that runs tandemd, as a list of strings. When nil, use "tandemd" from variable @code{exec-path}, or else the binary that "make daemon" builds next to this package.

@item tandem-daemon-idle-timeout
@vindex tandem-daemon-idle-timeout
Default: @code{600}.  Seconds the daemon keeps running with no Emacs connected. Zero keeps it running until you stop it.  Applies to daemons that Emacs starts.

@item tandem-daemon-start-timeout
@vindex tandem-daemon-start-timeout
Default: @code{10}.  Seconds to wait for a newly started daemon to accept connections.

@item tandem-daemon-transport
@vindex tandem-daemon-transport
Default: @code{unix}.  How Emacs reaches the daemon. unix: a Unix socket.  tcp: a port on this machine only, which the daemon writes with a secret token to an endpoint file; Emacs on Windows has no Unix sockets.

@item tandem-do-actions
@vindex tandem-do-actions
Default: @code{(("Refactor" . "Refactor this code to...}.  Instructions @code{tandem-do} offers, as (NAME . INSTRUCTION). You can always type your own instead.

@item tandem-environment-variables
@vindex tandem-environment-variables
Default: @code{("ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" "ANTHROPIC_AUTH_...}.  Environment variables each new session takes from Emacs. Claude Code reads its credentials and provider from these.  A new session gets the value Emacs has now (see @code{getenv}), or the variable removed if Emacs has none, whatever the daemon started with.  So after [setenv], a new chat ([universal-argument] [tandem]) uses the new value without restarting the daemon.  Other variables come from the daemon, which inherited them from the Emacs that started it.

@item tandem-events-buffer-size
@vindex tandem-events-buffer-size
Default: @code{2000000}.  Maximum size in characters of the protocol log buffer. Zero turns the log off; nil keeps everything.

@item tandem-focus-guard-seconds
@vindex tandem-focus-guard-seconds
Default: @code{3}.  Seconds after you use a window during which Claude leaves it alone.

@item tandem-instruction-files
@vindex tandem-instruction-files
Default: @code{("CLAUDE.md" "CLAUDE.local.md" ".clau...}.  Files that give a folder instructions of its own for Claude.

@item tandem-instructions
@vindex tandem-instructions
Default: @code{"Write in clear, simple English: shor...}.  Standing instructions Claude follows in every answer of a new chat. They go into Claude's system prompt, so they hold for every message without being repeated.  Empty for none.

@item tandem-layout-tab
@vindex tandem-layout-tab
Default: @code{"Claude"}.  Name of the tab @code{tandem} shows the chat in, or nil for the current tab. Claude's windows live where its chat is, so with a tab of its own your other tabs keep their layout.

@item tandem-magit-diff-limit
@vindex tandem-magit-diff-limit
Default: @code{60000}.  Most characters of the staged diff Claude reads for a commit message.

@item tandem-magit-draft-automatically
@vindex tandem-magit-draft-automatically
Default: @code{nil}.  Non-nil to draft the message whenever a commit buffer opens empty.

@item tandem-magit-model
@vindex tandem-magit-model
Default: @code{"haiku"}.  Model that drafts commit messages; nil for Claude Code's default.

@item tandem-magit-trailer
@vindex tandem-magit-trailer
Default: @code{nil}.  Trailer added to a commit message when the staged changes hold Claude's lines. Nil, the default, adds none.  For example:   "Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@@anthropic.com>"

@item tandem-markdown-modes
@vindex tandem-markdown-modes
Default: @code{(("py" . python-mode) ("python" . pyt...}.  Major modes for the languages named after ``` in the chat. A language not listed uses LANG-mode, or LANG-ts-mode, when one exists.

@item tandem-max-windows
@vindex tandem-max-windows
Default: @code{5}.  Most windows Claude's frame may have when Claude adds one. The chat window counts.  Claude never splits beyond this; at the limit it reuses a window instead.  Windows you make yourself are not limited.

@item tandem-mention-max-files
@vindex tandem-mention-max-files
Default: @code{5000}.  Most project files @@ completion offers.

@item tandem-mention-max-lines
@vindex tandem-mention-max-lines
Default: @code{400}.  Most lines of a buffer or region a mention attaches.

@item tandem-min-windows
@vindex tandem-min-windows
Default: @code{2}.  Fewest windows Claude leaves when it closes one, the chat included.

@item tandem-model
@vindex tandem-model
Default: @code{nil}.  Model for new sessions, such as "opus", or nil for Claude Code's default.

@item tandem-notes-automatic
@vindex tandem-notes-automatic
Default: @code{t}.  Non-nil to write a note on each commit made with Magit, and read notes on visit.

@item tandem-notes-ref
@vindex tandem-notes-ref
Default: @code{"refs/notes/tandem"}.  The git notes ref that holds Claude's lines.

@item tandem-org-answer-heading
@vindex tandem-org-answer-heading
Default: @code{"Claude's answer"}.  Title of the subheading Claude's answer goes under.

@item tandem-plan-mode-hook
@vindex tandem-plan-mode-hook
Default: @code{nil}.  Hook run after entering or leaving @code{tandem-plan-mode}. No problems result if this variable is not bound. @code{add-hook} automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)

@item tandem-popup-delay
@vindex tandem-popup-delay
Default: @code{0.3}.  Idle seconds in a hunk before its popup opens; nil opens it only on \[tandem-popup-show].

@item tandem-popup-style
@vindex tandem-popup-style
Default: @code{auto}.  How the popup shows: @code{auto}, @code{child-frame}, @code{inline} or nil for never. @code{auto} uses a child frame in graphical frames and the hunk's banner line elsewhere; @code{inline} always uses the banner line.

@item tandem-project-markers
@vindex tandem-project-markers
Default: @code{("CLAUDE.md" "CLAUDE.local.md" ".clau...}.  Files or folders that mark a project's root when it is not a repository.

@item tandem-project-root
@vindex tandem-project-root
Default: @code{vc}.  How to pick the folder a chat starts in, inside a repository. @code{vc}: the repository's root. @code{nearest-instructions}: the nearest folder at or above the file, inside the repository, with its own instructions (see @code{tandem-instruction-files}), else the repository's root. @code{ask}: ask, offering the repository's root and that folder. A function: called with no arguments in the current buffer; it returns a folder, or nil to fall back to @code{vc}.

@item tandem-resume-limit
@vindex tandem-resume-limit
Default: @code{50}.  Most earlier chats @code{tandem-resume} lists.

@item tandem-review-autosave
@vindex tandem-review-autosave
Default: @code{t}.  Whether to save a buffer after applying Claude's edit to it. Even when non-nil, a buffer is saved only if it had no unsaved changes of yours, so nothing of yours is ever saved behind your back.

@item tandem-review-merge-gap
@vindex tandem-review-merge-gap
Default: @code{2}.  Unchanged lines between two changes up to which they make one hunk.

@item tandem-review-note-lines
@vindex tandem-review-note-lines
Default: @code{3}.  Lines of Claude's answer a folded note shows. Notes start unfolded, with the whole answer; [fold] folds one.

@item tandem-review-style
@vindex tandem-review-style
Default: @code{blocking}.  How Claude's edits wait for you. @code{blocking}: Claude waits for your decision on each edit. @code{deferred}: Claude is told the edit waits for your review and carries on; your decisions go to Claude with your next message. @code{auto-accept}: edits are applied as they arrive, still coloured as Claude's, and undone like any change.

@item tandem-slash-popup
@vindex tandem-slash-popup
Default: @code{t}.  Non-nil to list the slash commands as soon as you type / to start a message.

@item tandem-socket-path
@vindex tandem-socket-path
Default: @code{nil}.  Socket the daemon listens on, or nil for the default. The default is $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tandem/daemon.sock.  The directory holding the socket must be private to you (mode 700). With @code{tandem-daemon-transport} set to tcp, this is the endpoint file instead, %LOCALAPPDATA%\tandem\daemon.json by default on Windows.

@item tandem-suggest-after
@vindex tandem-suggest-after
Default: @code{1500}.  How many characters after the cursor Claude sees.

@item tandem-suggest-before
@vindex tandem-suggest-before
Default: @code{4000}.  How many characters before the cursor Claude sees.

@item tandem-suggest-delay
@vindex tandem-suggest-delay
Default: @code{0.8}.  Seconds without typing before Claude is asked for a suggestion.

@item tandem-suggest-mode-hook
@vindex tandem-suggest-mode-hook
Default: @code{nil}.  Hook run after entering or leaving @code{tandem-suggest-mode}. No problems result if this variable is not bound. @code{add-hook} automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)

@item tandem-suggest-model
@vindex tandem-suggest-model
Default: @code{"claude-haiku-5-5"}.  The model suggestions use: a fast, cheap one.

@item tandem-tools-max-results
@vindex tandem-tools-max-results
Default: @code{60}.  Most results a tool lists.

@item tandem-tools-wait
@vindex tandem-tools-wait
Default: @code{3}.  Seconds a tool waits for a checker that is still running.

@item tandem-worktree-directory
@vindex tandem-worktree-directory
Default: @code{"@{repo@}.worktrees/@{name@}"}.  Where a new worktree goes, relative to the repository's parent folder. @{repo@} is the repository's folder name and @{name@} the worktree's.

@end table
